# K3: the A/B for the slide. c2-packed-tp4-speed-noslide is c2-packed-tp4-speed with QWEN_FAST_TP_KV_SLIDE=0: audits off, the
# six-op eager publication chain of v140. The same four tests as K2, so the difference between K2 and K3 is the slide's saving on
# the same prompts (expect about 300 ms per ramp user per round: ramp kv_history.prepare about 310 ms against about 5 ms). With K1
# (audits on, slide on) the three smokes separate the two new flags: K2 against K3 is the slide, K2 against K1 is the audits.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min; tests 8-25 min (v140's eager ramp rounds ran about 800 ms): 15 / 30 /
# 60 min.
# Read: as K2, in particular kv in [PACKED-PUBLISH] for the two ramp users (pool slots 2 and 3) and the 4-live wall.
# SOFT: a failure does not stop the window; the exactness jobs judge the text.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-noslide
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,warm_lifecycle,coding,concurrent4
